# Save plans in the repo

When you produce a plan (e.g. via the plan/CreatePlan flow), also persist it
into this repo at `.cursor/plans/` so it is version-controlled alongside the code.

- Write the plan to `.cursor/plans/<slug>.plan.md` (use the `*.plan.md` suffix to
  match the existing files in that folder).
- Use a short, descriptive kebab-case slug for `<slug>`.
- Keep YAML frontmatter consistent with the other plans (`name`, `overview`,
  `status`, `isProject`).
- If a plan tool wrote the file elsewhere (e.g. a global Cursor projects dir),
  copy it into `.cursor/plans/` here as well — the repo copy is the source of truth.

## This is allowed in plan mode

Writing the plan `.md` into `.cursor/plans/` is a **markdown edit**, which plan
mode permits — do it as part of producing the plan. Do **not** skip this rule on
the assumption that plan mode is read-only; only non-markdown edits and other
system changes are off-limits there. If you're unsure, write the markdown plan
file rather than deferring it.
